question:
\$ABCD\$ has side length \$13\$, and s \$E\$ and \$F\$ are exterior to the square such that \$BE=DF=5\$ and \$AE=CF=12\$. Find \$EF^{2}\$.
<asy>unitsize(0.2 cm);
pair A, B, C, D, E, F;
A = (0,13);
B = (13,13);
C = (13,0);
D = (0,0);
E = A + (12*12/13,5*12/13);
F = D + (5*5/13,-5*12/13);
draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);
draw(A--E--B);
draw(C--F--D);
dot("$A$", A, W);
dot("$B$", B, dir(0));
dot("$C$", C, dir(0));
dot("$D$", D, W);
dot("$E$", E, N);
dot("$F$", F, S);</asy>
